.TH TGCLI 1
.SH NAME
tgcli \- Telegram command-line client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tgcli
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tgcli
uses a per-account daemon for Telegram operations. Client-local metadata commands
do not read account configuration or contact the daemon.
.SH RAW SUBSET
.B tgcli raw -
reads one JSON request from standard input and invokes only the function subset
admitted by the pinned reviewed policy. The current policy admits 54 typed
functions and denies the other 947 whole. Raw is not access to the full TDLib
API. Write-tier functions require the normal write grant; destructive functions
also require confirmation. Request and response bodies are never stored in the
raw audit log.
.SH SHELL COMPLETION
.B tgcli completion bash
prints the byte-stable Bash 3.2-compatible completion asset.
.PP
.B tgcli completion zsh
prints the byte-stable zsh completion asset.
.PP
.B tgcli completion fish
prints the byte-stable fish completion asset.
.PP
The assets are generated from the canonical public-command registry. They do not
execute tgcli or read configuration. The
.B --no-color
option and a nonempty
.B NO_COLOR
environment variable do not alter their bytes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I share/bash-completion/completions/tgcli
Bash completion asset.
.TP
.I share/zsh/site-functions/_tgcli
zsh completion asset.
.TP
.I share/fish/vendor_completions.d/tgcli.fish
fish completion asset.
.TP
.I share/tgcli/public-command-registry.json
Canonical command registry used to generate the installed completion assets.
